      "writtenOn": "2021-12-02T23:44:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like the idea verifying the battery manufacturer and device name in the NO_AUTO_DETECT path.  However, this code as is will increment past the board selected index, potentially matching to another battery in the list.\n\nI think it\u0027s clearer if you explicitly check only the index returned by board_get_default_battery_type().\n\nSomething like:\n\n#if defined(CONFIG_BATTERY_TYPE_NO_AUTO_DETECT)\n    battery_type \u003d board_get_default_battery_type();\n    fuel_gauge \u003d \u0026board_battery_info[battery_type].fuel_gauge;\n    if (strcasecmp(manuf_name, fuel_gauge-\u003emanuf_name))\n        /* manufacturer mismatch */\n        battery_type \u003d BATTERY_TYPE_COUNT;\n    if (strncasecmp(device_name, fuel_gauge-\u003edevice_name,len))\n        /* device mismatch\n\tbattery_type \u003d BATTERY_TYPE_COUNT\n#else\n    /* Loop through board_battery_info[] */\n#endif",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "39e8520d639f8a542f2a170a302305f6b9358c48",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9dfb815d_6559378f",
        "filename": "common/battery_fuel_gauge.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-03T17:23:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another alternative: board_get_default_battery_type() could return a special value to indicate that auto-detect can still be performed.\n\nFor example:\nboard_get_default_battery() {\n    if (BOARD_ID \u003d\u003d 1)\n        /* Force 2 cell */\n        return BATTERY_GETAC_SMP_HHP_408_2S;\n    if (BOARD_ID \u003d\u003d 2)\n        /* Force 3 cell */\n        return BATTERY_GETAC_SMP_HHP_408_3S;\n       \n    /* All other boards - auto-detect the battery */ \n    return BATTERY_TYPE_COUNT;\n}\n\nIf the returned value is BATTERY_TYPE_COUNT, walk the board_battery_info[] array to find the correct battery.  Otherwise, validate the manufacturer and device of the selected index only.  Failing if there is a mismatch.",
      "parentUuid": "f045542f_74e2246e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "39e8520d639f8a542f2a170a302305f6b9358c48",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
